# RHEL 9.7 private md headers (drivers/md/)
#
# EXACT copy of the RHEL 9.7 kernel's drivers/md/ headers, extracted from the
# kernel-5.14.0-611.42.1.el9_7 source RPM.  Same vendoring rule as md-vanilla/
# (see its README for the bitmap_ops-vtable lesson): always the *target
# kernel's* exact drivers/md/, never a mainline approximation.
#
# Despite the 5.14 base, el9_7 carries the 6.12-era md core backport:
# md_submodule registration, bitmap_ops vtable, md_init_stacking_limits /
# queue_limits_*.  Deltas vs md-vanilla (6.12.90) are small: struct mddev
# adds cluster_ops (no raidkm-visible offset pins change without re-checking
# BTF — see the BUILD_BUG_ON block in km/raid_km.c and tools/check-mddev-abi.sh),
# mddev_lock/trylock return -ENODEV on MD_DELETED, rdev_blocked() helper.
#
# raidkm on RHEL 9 builds against these via TARGET=rhel9
# (compat/compat-rhel9.h).
#
# Files: md.h md-bitmap.h md-cluster.h raid1.h raid5.h raid10.h
